'''Zamboanga Sibugay's 2nd congressional district''' is one of the two [[congressional districts of the Philippines]] in the province of [[Zamboanga Sibugay]]. It has been represented in the [[House of Representatives of the Philippines|House of Representatives]] since 2007.<ref name="congleg">{{cite web|url=http://www.congress.gov.ph/legislators/?v=province |title=Roster of Philippine legislators |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=February 19, 2021}}</ref> It was created after the 2006 reapportionment that divided the province into two congressional districts.<ref name="apportion">{{cite web|url=https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph/2006/10/26/republic-act-no-9360/ |title=Republic Act No. 9360 |date=26 October 2006 |publisher=[[Official Gazette (Philippines)]] |accessdate=February 19, 2021}}</ref> The district is composed of the provincial capital, [[Ipil, Zamboanga Sibugay|Ipil]], and the western municipalities of [[Kabasalan]], [[Naga, Zamboanga Sibugay|Naga]], [[Roseller Lim, Zamboanga Sibugay|Roseller Lim]], [[Siay]], [[Titay]] and [[Tungawan]].  It is currently represented in the [[20th Congress of the Philippines|20th Congress]] by [[Marly Hofer–Hasim]] of the [[Partido Federal ng Pilipinas]].<ref name="congmem">{{cite web|url=http://www.congress.gov.ph/members/ |title=House Members |publisher=[[House of Representatives of the Philippines]] |accessdate=February 19, 2021}}</ref>

